{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793357866,"nonce":"Xouw3wrqEMsASbPDDMOR86XOn28=","title":"Declared Rust 1.85 MSRV disagrees with let chains and advisory Rust 1.75 CI","message":"Cargo.toml declares rust-version 1.85, while compiled core/layout/app source uses let chains, stabilized in Rust 1.88. Examples include core/src/reactive.rs, layout/src/renderer/cursor.rs and app/src/context/css_cache_lifecycle.rs. Edition 2024 alone already excludes the workflow compiler 1.75.\n\n.github/workflows/msrv.yml installs Rust 1.75, runs cargo check --workspace --all-targets, and sets continue-on-error: true. It therefore cannot enforce the advertised minimum compiler for the intended release. Release work must choose and document the supported MSRV, align the manifest and a required scoped CI check, or remove syntax/dependencies above the existing promise. Do not claim that raising the version alone verifies every release crate/feature/target.\n\nScoped evidence: CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2 cargo +1.88 check --locked --offline -p blinc_core --lib --target-dir /private/tmp/blinc-release-msrv passed; the equivalent command selecting blinc_gpu, blinc_layout and blinc_app libraries passed. Logs /private/tmp/blinc-release-api-core-msrv188.log and /private/tmp/blinc-release-api-msrv188.log. Existing unknown-lint warnings for mismatched_lifetime_syntaxes occur on 1.88. No Rust 1.85 toolchain was installed for a complete check; the syntax requirement itself disproves 1.85 support. No workspace gate or CI edits were made during review, and this check does not certify the full 25-crate release cohort.\n\nReference: https://blog.rust-lang.org/2025/06/26/Rust-1.88.0/","files":null}]}